<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chinchaysuyu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chinchay Suyu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chinchaysuyu was the north-western and most populous of the four quarters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a>, stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> through the central Andes and coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> into Ecuador and southern Colombia. It included the former Chimú kingdom and the northern cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomebamba">Tumebamba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chinchaysuyu.jpg" alt="Chinchaysuyu" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: L'Américain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinchaysuyu_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
